From d756145d28f8270417ca62569efe736cd8546952 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 00:08:24 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] test: add bounded WebTransport loss experiment tooling
 without enabling defaults

Port the original UDP impairment prototype with independently seeded packet
loss, serialized per-direction rate, fixed delay and bounded pending packet
and byte storage. Keep it loopback-only and single-client, with counters,
owned cleanup and a main guard. Never pretend TCP stream byte dropping is
packet loss.

Add an explicit single-case WT/WSS real-node driver using fresh artificial
regtest fixture copies, a real next block, fresh ping completion samples and
matched valid Avalanche response timing. Require an audited external packet
impairment receipt for a TCP comparison. Share one work budget across node
startup, connection, transfer and RPC socket waits. Record raw samples,
binary/tool hashes, peer counters, load and incomplete status. Matrix preview
starts no processes; one case never declares the full gate passed.

Native combined build passes 23 actions; focused observation assertion
rebuild passes 7 actions. Four poll/response cases pass 383 assertions,
including exact valid RTT event text and absence of rejected-response samples.
Twelve deterministic Python checks and Ruff pass. Tiny WT/WSS node smokes and
one UDP echo pass with owned cleanup; they explicitly lack full latency data
and do not measure performance. Preserve the first failed fixture and its
source/timeout diagnosis. Final post-smoke source guard only shortens the
remaining budget after JSON encoding and has a negative control.

Leave compile/runtime transport defaults OFF and bulk preference at 1: Linux
loss/CPU, Guix, browser stock/public-CA, proxy, soak, sanitizers and Safari
gates were not run or remain incomplete. No benchmark sweep, production
operation, trust-store change or rendezvous implementation was added.
